---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Headroom"
  description="A native iOS app I'm building, solo, in SwiftUI."
>
  <article class="headroom">
    <header class="headroom__header">
      <p class="headroom__status">
        <span class="headroom__status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        In development
      </p>
      <h1>Headroom</h1>
      <p class="headroom__subtitle">
        A native iOS app I'm building, solo, in SwiftUI.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="headroom__body">
      <h2>What it does</h2>
      <p>
        Headroom shows you what you actually have to spare after your
        committed expenses, not just your raw balance. Most finance apps show
        you a number. I wanted to show you a decision.
      </p>

      <h2>Why native, not cross-platform</h2>
      <p>
        I built it in SwiftUI instead of React Native or Expo. I wanted real
        design craft, widgets, and Face ID, the things you only get by
        building for the platform instead of around it. I'm also
        deliberately avoiding Apple's TabView and NavigationStack, since iOS
        26's Liquid Glass styling overrides custom visual identity if you use
        the system components. I wanted the app to look like Headroom, not
        like every other app that shipped this year.
      </p>

      <h2>The AI architecture</h2>
      <p>
        There are three layers, and each one only does what it's actually
        good at. Deterministic Swift handles the calculations, because money
        math should never be probabilistic. Apple's on-device Foundation
        Models handle intent and labeling, fast and private, no network call.
        Anthropic's API handles the judgment calls that need real-world
        knowledge, the ones a pattern-matcher on-device can't reason about.
      </p>

      <h2>Why CSV import, not Open Banking</h2>
      <p>
        V1 imports a bank statement as a CSV instead of connecting through an
        account aggregator. That's not a shortcut, it's a decision: no FCA
        AISP licensing, no third-party aggregator fees, and I can honestly
        say your data never leaves your device. I'd rather ship something
        true and narrow than something that only sounds secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it's at</h2>
      <p>
        In active development. I'm currently tweaking the AI response
        quality and planning the CSV import onboarding flow next.
      </p>

      <h2>Follow along</h2>
      <p>
        The code is public: <a href="https://github.com/rxzir/finance-buddy"
          >https://github.com/rxzir/finance-buddy</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/" class="headroom__back">&larr; Back</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .headroom__header {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .headroom__status {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }

  .headroom__status-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    animation: headroom-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .headroom__status-dot {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  @keyframes headroom-pulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 1;
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }
  }

  .headroom__header h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .headroom__subtitle {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .headroom__body {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .headroom__body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .headroom__body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .headroom__body a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .headroom__back {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .headroom__back:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
</style>
